{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Am]Alas my [C]love, you [G]do me [Em]wrong,
to [Am]cast me off [E]discourteously.
For [Am]I have [C]loved [G]you so [Em]long,
[Am]delighting [E7]in your [Am]company.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Greensleeves was [G]all my [Em]joy,
[Am]Greensleeves was [E]my delight,
[C]Greensleeves was my [G]heart of [Em]gold,
and [Am]who but my [E7]Lady [Am]Greensleeves.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I [Am]have been [C]readie [G]at your [Em]hand,
to [Am]grant what ever [E]you would crave.
I [Am]have both [C]waged [G]life and [Em]land,
your [Am]love and good [E7]will for to [Am]have.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Thy [Am]gown was [C]of the [G]grassy [Em]green,
thy [Am]sleeves of satin [E]hanging by,
Which [Am]made thee [C]be our [G]harvest [Em]queen,
[Am]And yet thou [E7]wouldst not [Am]love me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Greensleeves was [G]all my [Em]joy,
[Am]Greensleeves was [E]my delight,
[C]Greensleeves was my [G]heart of [Em]gold,
and [Am]who but my [E7]Lady [Am]Greensleeves.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Well, [Am]I will [C]pray to [G]God on [Em]high,
That [Am]thou constancy [E]mayst see,
And [Am]that yet [C]once [G]before I [Em]die,
[Am]Thou wilt [E7]vouchsafe to [Am]love me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: End Chorus}
[C]Greensleeves, now [G]farewel [Em]adue,
[Am]God I pray to [E]prosper thee:
For [C]I am stil thy [G]lover [Em]true,
[Am]come once [E7]againe and [Am]love me.
